  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.3. Increased institutional capacity and resilience of labour administrations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour inspection was restructured in 2022 and is under the mandate of the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection.

Strategic compliance planning (SCP) was introduced to labour inspection, and the 2023 labour inspection plan was developed based on SCP adopted in April 2023. This is the first labour inspection workplan after the mandate of labour inspection moved to the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection. Child labour was officially included in the labour inspection checklist. Workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; representatives were actively engaged in the SCP.

 The ILO,  with funding from the European Union, made the following contributions: 
&#x2022;	Provided technical comments on the draft law on State Inspection and draft concept note on the draft law on Employment Promotion 
&#x2022;	 Supported the Ministry of Labour and Social Protection (MLSP) in the preparation of the ratification of ILO C81 and C129 process, including conducting a comparative analysis of laws and preparing a concept note to facilitate the ratification.
&#x2022;	Technical support in developing a transition plan for transferring labour inspection responsibilities from the General Agency for Specialized Inspection(GASI) to the MLSP, while ensuring the development of a labour inspection policy/strategy that aligns with international labour standards.
&#x2022;	Providing capacity development support to MLSP in effectively applying the Labour Law, newly revised checklists, and international labour standards during the transfer of labour inspection responsibilities from the GASI to MLSP. In May 2023, 130 labour inspectors were trained on the regulatory framework and international labour standards.
&#x2022;	Enhancing the quality of labour inspection in high-risk sectors through the introduction of the Strategic Compliance Planning methodology for labour inspection planning. This methodology was applied continuously at MLSP in 2023 for the development of the annual labour inspection plan.
&#x2022;	Upgraded the occupational accidents and acute poisoning registration system &#x2013; om.inspection.gov.mn
&#x2022;	Contributed to improving labour inspection quality in high-risk sectors by introducing the Strategic Compliance Planning methodology in the planning of the labour inspection plan
&#x2022;	Contributed to creating decent working conditions in high-risk sectors. Around 1000 employers and workers were trained on law compliance. A self-assessment monitoring tool is developed for enterprises. Monitoring exercises on law compliance are conducted by the trade unions.</narrative>
   </description>
